From 3510c59d6effa4b4e71c80847a26364d3b7d9a6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:34:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: one worker queue (pool:worker) instead of
 pinning cards to single workers

Portable cards queued for one machine froze the choice when capacity changed: on 11-12 ten
ready cards waited up to 261 min on machine:worker-2 while it was drain-held and worker-1 and
worker-4 had free slots (t_01a1ce6551c811ef).

- kanban.placement.worker_queue[<gateway>] = "pool:worker": a portable card created on that
  gateway (tool or CLI, no explicit runs_on/pin) gets runs_on [pool:worker, *coordination
  labels] instead of the worker-first-v1 machine reservation, while some active, unheld machine
  carries the label. The reservation code stays for rollback.
- heavy_route accepts a label value: emitted as is; live when some active unheld machine has it.
- `hermes kanban move <id> --pool` (= --runs-on pool:worker). A move to machine:<x> where x is a
  pool worker needs host_reason (--host-reason / kanban_move host_reason), recorded on the
  event. A pooled card re-pinned to the worker it is on is refused while its workspace is clean
  and pushed; unpushed/dirty state is recorded as unpushed_state.
- run-machine accounting treats a pool:worker card as POOL.
